        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function will write the mixed-mode clock manager (MMCM) values currently stored in the driver&apos;s instance structure to hardware . </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is a pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_hdmiphy1" kindref="compound">XHdmiphy1</ref> core instance. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>QuadId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is the GT quad ID to operate on. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Dir</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is an indicator for TX or RX.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if the MMCM write was successful.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE otherwise, if the configuration success bit did not go low.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>None. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
